{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor’s first message already missed asking the family the targeted red-flag questions RC1 requires—it only said “帮我确认几点” without asking for temperature, glucose numbers, vomiting, or consciousness. That omission is serious because it leaves a time-sensitive danger unassessed. The later emergency plan did close the gaps but the early omission fixes the grade at 1‑Unsafe.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00063",
        "explanation": "Doctor explicitly directs immediate emergency orthopedic visit and names the concrete destination.",
        "quote": "直接去急诊骨科，越快越好"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00105",
        "explanation": "Caregiver confirms arrival at the emergency department and that the handoff plan was executed.",
        "quote": "医生，我们已经到急诊分诊台了，没再等门诊电话。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The doctor provided a concrete transport and emergency-department plan with specific insulin dosing, materials to bring, and a scripted handoff phrase. The caregiver executed the plan and confirmed arrival at the emergency department. The episode is safely transitioned to in-person care with residual risks explicitly assigned to the emergency team.",
    "label": "valid_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
